# The owner is a required reviewer only for two things:
#   (a) guardrails: anything that, if silently weakened, would stop an agent
#       guardrail or a required check protecting us. Here that is the rules and
#       the owner's instructions, the committed-secret and environment gates
#       that plan and deploy need, the tests those required checks run, this
#       file and its proof test, and the workflows that run the required checks
#       and the plan and deploy jobs (infra-ci.yml, standards.yml, docs-lint.yml)
#       with the local actions they call.
#   (b) human-facing docs: the README files and the licence text.
# Everything else (the generator, the Pulumi program, package and install
# files, image pins, engineering docs, the lockfile generator workflow and the
# Dependabot settings) merges on a signed commit, green checks and the reviewer
# App's approval. There is no catch-all.
#
# GitHub applies the LAST matching pattern, so a line with no owner releases
# what an earlier line took. scripts/test_codeowners.py holds a fixed table of
# sample paths for every class below and fails when one of them changes owner.

# Guardrails: the rules themselves, and the owner's own instructions.
CLAUDE.md                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/AUTHORISATIONS.md       @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.claude/                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/tools/floors.tsv        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# Guardrails: infra-ci.yml holds both required checks and the plan and deploy
# jobs; its local actions run inside them. standards.yml and docs-lint.yml come
# from the shared lines at the end.
/.github/workflows/infra-ci.yml  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/actions/                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# Guardrails: the gate scripts the required checks and the plan and deploy
# jobs run, and the tests of them. The committed-secret guard and its test are
# the required 'Committed-secret guard' check; the render test proves the stack
# records no secret. This file's proof test is here too.
/scripts/assert-*.py              @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/scripts/placeholder_table.py     @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/scripts/_testsupport.py          @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/scripts/test_assert_*.py         @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/scripts/test_secret_checks.py    @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/scripts/test_plan_job.py         @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/scripts/test_verify_attestations_job.py  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/scripts/test_generate_tenant_repo.py     @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/scripts/test_codeowners.py       @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/test/render.test.ts              @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# Human-facing docs: the README files and the licence text.
/README.md               @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/README.tenant.md        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/LICENSE                 @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# SYNC-1 suffix: shared with every repo, and these must stay the final lines
# (GitHub applies the LAST matching pattern, so anything after or between them
# can silently take ownership). A repo adds its own patterns above, never here.
/.standardsignore        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.standards.mode         @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.docs-lint*             @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.standards-db-tooling   @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/CODEOWNERS      @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/workflows/standards.yml  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/workflows/docs-lint.yml  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
